  "step_1": "The decision reason involves adjusting the probabilities of outcomes that have a probability below 20% by increasing them by 10 percentage points (i.e., adding 0.10 to the probability). Then, it computes a weighted sum of outcomes using these adjusted probabilities and prefers the lottery with the higher weighted sum. In this decision problem, both lotteries have probabilities below 20%: Lottery A has 0.2% (0.002) and Lottery B has 0.1% (0.001), both below 20%. Therefore, the reason can be applied. After applying the weight adjustment: \n- For Lottery A: adjusted probability = 0.002 + 0.10 = 0.102, weighted outcome = 3000 × 0.102 = 306\n- For Lottery B: adjusted probability = 0.001 + 0.10 = 0.101, weighted outcome = 6000 × 0.101 = 606\nThus, according to the reason, Lottery B has a higher weighted sum and would be preferred. The reason prefers B over A.",
